WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.010
A fully-actuated unmanned aerial vehicle serves as the experimental platform to execute physical interaction tasks.

2
00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:12.010
The onboard force-torque sensor at the manipulator base provides direct force measurements at sixty hertz.

3
00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:18.390
At the end-effector tip, a GelSight vision-based tactile sensor captures optical tactile images at thirty hertz.

4
00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:25.130
Optical flow tracks the motion of printed markers to capture the deformation of the elastomer gel pad.

5
00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:31.140
A k-nearest neighbors model then estimates the contact force directly from these marker displacement features.

6
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:37.890
A Kalman filter fuses the force-torque sensor measurements and tactile estimates to obtain the measured contact force.

7
00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:45.000
In parallel, a ResNet-18 neural network processes the full tactile image to determine contact and recognize surface textures.

8
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.010
The classification output identifies the contact texture and generates a discrete contact detection switching signal.

9
00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:56.270
A motion capture system provides high-rate position measurements at one hundred eighty hertz.

10
00:00:56.270 --> 00:01:03.020
The force controller computes the force tracking control effort using the fused contact force and reference force.

11
00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:09.020
Simultaneously, a position controller calculates the motion control command based on reference and measured positions.

12
00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:15.770
A selection matrix dynamically blends the motion and force control commands based on the contact detection state.

13
00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:22.890
Finally, the control allocation module maps the combined wrench command into individual rotor speeds for the fully-actuated vehicle.

